# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Re-arms what each hand held, out of the backpack, when a cast or a disarm empties it.
# A cast clears the hands: the weapon lands in the backpack and the fight goes on with
# fists until it is back (user check on the archer, 2026-10-21, and the gather loops
# before it). Both hand layers are read every two seconds. Razor's lefthand is the
# two-handed layer and its righthand the one-handed layer, so the layer an item was seen
# on is the hand it goes back to: no weapon kind is named, and a word cannot live in a
# variable anyway (document/scripting/razor.md part 3). Each layer remembers the item it
# held by serial, so a replacement armed by hand is remembered the same way, and a looted
# twin in the backpack is never mistaken for it. rearm_graphic adds a backpack search for
# a fresh client, when nothing is remembered yet: the setup list below says which
# graphics are two-handed, by the wiki weapon table, so the search knows the hand.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ config
#
#   config__rearm_graphic
#      Graphic of the weapon to pick out of the backpack while both hands are empty and
#      nothing is remembered, on a fresh client. 0 picks nothing: only an item once seen
#      in hand goes back. The hand it goes to comes from the two-handed list in setup.
#      5042 is the bow, 5187 the two handed axe and 31186 the Rampart Crossbow in
#      document/game/item-list.md.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! config__rearm_graphic 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   interval__equip_retry
#      How often the hands are read. A refused equip, after a disarm for example, waits
#      this long before the next try.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! interval__equip_retry 2000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ timer
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
timer__equip interval__equip_retry


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__rearm_left, var__rearm_right
#      The serial last seen on the two-handed layer (lefthand) and on the one-handed layer
#      (righthand), kept across Stop and Play. 0 means nothing seen yet, or the item gone
#      from hand and backpack.
#
#   var__rearm_sent
#      Scratch: 1 once this check sent an equip, so the second hand waits for the next.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
if not varexist var__rearm_left
    @setvar! var__rearm_left 0
endif

if not varexist var__rearm_right
    @setvar! var__rearm_right 0
endif

@setvar! var__rearm_sent 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ setup
